      "value": "@{62df21399dbd2f44ab58492c|full_name}: I almost 100% sure that having some kind of vrca authentication feature like this would incredibly mitigate the ammount of vrca's directly uploaded to rippers accounts, the creators themselves have have already created way to mitigate the avatar package files leaking, the only real issue is people who just reuploaded the vrca directly to their accounts from someone they saw in public, and theres nothing the person can do. By adding a single bit of data/information to the vrca file that saves the username/id of the person who first uploaded that avatar (aka, created that vrca file) and adding an authentication step that checks if the vrca file you're trying to upload already has that information and if it does it blocks it from uploading. By Doing something like that you can mitigate vrca reuploads extremely well.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
