      "value": "@{600f0e36b257ed443f54f640|full_name}: again that's not how .vrca files work. vrca files are technically an encrypted file formate that the local VRChat client reads and puts into your computer. It's essentially an ID. what you're asking for is literally not possible for VRChat to even do, and even then it'd be a major waste of time since there are programs out there that will be able to decrypt the file anyway. It's not gonna work the way you want it to sadly",
