      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Vrca already has Id of avatar where it should be uploaded, and if it missmatch, it will not load. So just reuploading vrca as is will not work, you will get \"error avatar\". This check exist for like at least 2 years now. Rippers actually building new version of vrca when stealing.\n\nBut yea, more security is required for sure. Like encryption or something idunno...\n\nAs for now vrca and vrcw it's just plain asset bundles, which is loadable not only by ripping tools, but also by unity editor itself. (yes it is possible to \"rip\" using editor itself).",
