      "value": "@{5f30a4580d85f347c361e55d|full_name}: To be completely truthful, there's honestly no real way to prevent ripping, especially given that VRChat is using Unity, a popular game engine with tools that can decompile unity asset bundles. For VRC to prevent ripping would be wasting a lot of R&D that could be used to improve creator tools like Physbones or add even new features we can't conceive of yet. But from that same blog post the thing that Tupper highlighted as well is that not even triple A studios can prevent asset ripping, and we even see those models run around VRChat as well. The best we can do is continue to submit reports until moderator action happens.",
